\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Complete AQMRG platform architecture showing the multi-tier data flow. Tiers are logically grouped by role, spanning from edge sensing to cloud-hosted analytics and event streaming via Apache Kafka.}}{9}{figure.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces End-to-end data lifecycle in a compact snaking layout. Timing annotations indicate typical systemic latency from physical sensing to global dashboard availability.}}{10}{figure.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Physical deployment topology showing the four hosting environments: a field-deployed Arduino node, PythonAnywhere's managed Python hosting, Vercel's edge CDN, and a Docker Compose cluster for microservices.}}{10}{figure.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Hardware wiring topology. Sensor modules connect to the Arduino Due via diverse interfaces (UART, I2C, Analog, Digital), with the SIM800L module providing cellular connectivity.}}{11}{figure.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Structure of the JSON telemetry payload transmitted from the Arduino Due to the Flask backend. Annotations indicate which downstream subsystem consumes each section.}}{12}{figure.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Firmware state machine governing the operational lifecycle of the edge node, including polling cycles and fault recovery logic.}}{13}{figure.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Flask application factory initialization flow. The system utilizes a singleton pattern for ML model loading during the WSGI server startup phase.}}{14}{figure.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Entity-Relationship diagram for the SQLite database. Each \texttt {SensorReading} stores raw sensor data plus all four prediction columns. \texttt {DeviceHealth} provides per-submission hardware diagnostics, and \texttt {DeviceMetadata} maintains persistent geographic identity per device.}}{15}{figure.8}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Ingestion pipeline logic flow. Each request is validated, passed through the ML ensemble, and asynchronously relayed to the live dashboard within the HTTP cycle.}}{16}{figure.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces ML training pipeline: raw CSV data undergoes cleaning and feature selection before being split into training/test sets. Three distinct algorithms are trained, cross-validated, and serialized for production deployment.}}{18}{figure.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces ML ensemble inference pipeline. Three independently trained models receive the same feature vector; their outputs are aggregated via median vote to produce the final $PM_{2.5}$ prediction.}}{19}{figure.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Ensemble aggregation decision logic. Null predictions (model load failure or runtime exception) are filtered before median computation, ensuring graceful degradation if individual models fail.}}{20}{figure.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Modular React.js component hierarchy. The architecture separates structural layout components from specialized visualization and diagnostic panels.}}{20}{figure.13}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Dashboard connection state machine. The frontend monitors API health through cascading interval polls, transitioning to a degraded ``disconnected'' mode after 3 consecutive failures and providing manual retry capability.}}{21}{figure.14}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Intelligence Monitor logic flow for real-time anomaly detection and visual state synchronisation.}}{22}{figure.15}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces The 9-step guided EDA workflow. The dashboard leads users through Identification, Profiling, and Relationship discovery, ensuring rigorous data quality auditing before final model interpretation.}}{23}{figure.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Mitigation Engine decision tree. The system performs cascading string pattern matching on hardware diagnostic telemetry to generate actionable troubleshooting advice.}}{24}{figure.17}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Containerized microservices topology. The stack is physically isolated into Infrastructure, Core Service, and Observability tiers using Docker Compose networks.}}{25}{figure.18}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces The Kafka-to-InfluxDB bridge flow for high-resolution time-series storage.}}{26}{figure.19}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Request-response sequence for ML forecast comparison.}}{27}{figure.20}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Arduino ingestion sequence diagram. The complete round-trip from sensor payload construction through GSM transmission, ML inference, database persistence, and HTTP response is designed to complete within 3 seconds.}}{28}{figure.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces The Observability stack for real-time monitoring and historical analysis.}}{29}{figure.22}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Comparative $R^2$ scores across the four model approaches. Gradient Boosting achieves the highest individual score (0.9715), while the median ensemble provides variance-reduced production stability.}}{29}{figure.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces RMSE comparison across models. The progression from Linear Regression (42.38) to Gradient Boosting (12.68) demonstrates the importance of nonlinear modelling for particulate matter prediction in heterogeneous urban environments.}}{30}{figure.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {25}{\ignorespaces Simplified repository structure showing the key directories and files across all four platform tiers.}}{32}{figure.25}%
